Z||000014||Cheever3000||08-29-2001||12:23 AM||||My neice worked at American Airlines in Dallas, and Carl Lewis came up asking where to catch his flight.  She pointed to a gate down the hall and said "If you run, you might make it!"  He laughed.<P>I myself have run across Bengal football players Icky Woods (before he got hurt), Chris Collinsworth, and Anthony Munoz, at the Mall, the hospital and the grocery store.<P>I coulda got Chuck Norris's autograph, but I figured if I leave him alone, he'll leave me alone!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Coconut||08-29-2001||01:02 AM||||When Kristina , me and my nephew went to one of the Cart races in Portland a few years back, this tall black fella on a scooter darn near tagged my 6 yr. old nephew while we were in the paddock area. I was a bit perturbed and said to him "You need to slow that thing down!" all the while thinking he looked vaguely familiar.<P>He stopped, made sure Chas was okay, apologized and went on his way.....about a minute later, it hit me.....we were close to the Payton-Coyne Racing area....Dangit! That was Walter Payton I just talked to! And I didn't even realize it! <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||wkayl||08-29-2001||01:11 AM||||I was at the Colorado National Speedway and Richard Petty was the flagman who started the race.  He was about 20 rows up in the press box looking out when I started waving to him.  After about 2 min of waving I caught his attention.  He looked at me like "Who is that crazy guy waving?"  He gave me a weak wave like "If I do this, maybe he will go away."<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
