Z||000032||Songman||08-29-2001||09:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR>Who is Peter Cetera?<BR>Ok Songman no sand baggin only im allowed to hold back because its my topic  If you dont tell about those other encounters Im gonna tell Cliff that you wont play right <BR><B> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Peter Cetera was the lead singer for Chicago, plus had a bit of a career as a solo artist as well...<P>Other encounters.. that would take a while! Since I did kinda grow up around show business... I've known just about everyone in the country music business for the past 35 years... plus, lots of people from other entertainment industries that are country fans... it has been a pretty cool ride...<BR>Probably if I had to name a couple of the coolest.. one would be Richard Petty. Got to spend a race at Talledega in his pits with him. And Earl Campbell from the Houston Oilers. We were playing down in Texas once and this big ole huge black man started to walk up on the stage. I grabbed him and told him he couldn't. He said, It's okay, he knows me. I still said he would have to wait till after the show. It was funny later on the bus when they were picking on me about how many guys had not been able to stop Earl from crossing a line and I did! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000033||Raydar||08-29-2001||09:20 AM||||Used to date Ben Jones' niece. Ben Jones being "Cooter" from the Dukes Of Hazzard and a Ga. Congressman. Also worked with his brother (her dad) for several years. Never got to meet Ben, though. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000034||ChadMan||08-29-2001||09:31 AM||||Funny and true:  In 1993 at the Mid-Ohio CART race, I was in the paddock men's room taking a whiz.  Out of the corner of my eye I see that the guy at the next stall looks familiar.  Well, obviously looking over at him would be a violation of men's room etiquette, so I waited until I went to the sink to turn back and look.  It was Gene Hackman -- he had part ownership in the Galles team!||||reg||10
Z||000035||stimpy||08-29-2001||09:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>Oh yeah? Well I stayed in a hotel where Miss Teen America was being held.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Against her will? Was it roger who had her locked up in there?<P>(You guys are making this too easy)<P>I met Chuck Berry. Well, not really "met" as he was shitty drunk, it being noon already. But I did get his autograph.  I also sold hotdogs to a couple of 49ers back 12 years ago when I used to run a vending cart. I was too stoned to remember who they were, but they were HUGE!||||reg||1
Z||000036||mbramble||08-29-2001||09:59 AM||||Oh yeah, the guy who sits right across from me at work is the brother of Andre Braugher who was Gideon on Gideon's Crossing, was in Law and Order and in quite a few movies. <P>And I too met Sky King when I was a youngun.  And John Provost, the kid who was on the original Lassie.  They were at some tourist place down in FL when we went down there on vacation.  Lots of years ago.<P>I also met Ian Botham when I was stationed in Scotland.  He's a famous cricket player.  We had just left Loch Ness where I had re-enlisted one of my Navy guys. We stopped at a pub and I recognized him when we walked in because he had been all over the TV recently for some fund raising walk.  I talked to one of his entourage and he introduced me and Ian invited me to sit down for a beer.  He was traveling from loch to loch in what was basically a yacht.  Tough life....<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||kslish||08-29-2001||10:14 AM||||I was driving to Nags Head, NC once and I was stuck in a traffic jam that wasn't moving at all.  Turns out there was a limo in front of me that was driving James (I feel GOOD!) Brown.  James got out of the limo to strecth for a while and I was the only one who recognized him.  It was fun chatting with him for a few minutes.  <P>That's the only celebrity I can think of besides Christina Aguleira since I have a friend that went to high school with her(Christina's from Western PA).  She's a real biatch in person.<P>Oh yeah, there are the various current and former Pittsburgh Steelers since I was their account exec for their cell phones and pagers up until last year.  <P>Also I spent an afternoon chatting a few years ago with Mario and Michael Andretti since they own a Toyota dealership in the Pittsburgh area that my Mom bought her car at.  Mario is cool, not to impressed with Michael....  <P>Ken S.||||reg||1
