Z||000056||Wolfhound||08-29-2001||05:33 PM||||fieronv, You rang a bell with the Earthwinds.<BR>A friend of mine at Auburn was Mark Kittinger. I knew him for years before I found out his dad was Joe Kittinger Who flew the first solo Atlantic crossing in a balloon. "The Rosie O'Grady". He also holds from the 1960,s the all time altitude record for a freefall parachute Jump!<BR>August 16th 1960<BR>102,800 ft. broke sound barrier in freefall.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000057||LT1 Chop Top||08-29-2001||06:24 PM||||I have met & hung out with Gary Numan, his wife and band several times over the last several years.  He actually likes Fiero's (my maroon one says "NUMAN" on the plate), and he thought his Cerbera was probably faster than my Chop Top.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/numa7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000058||c m west||08-29-2001||09:02 PM||||If any of you guys have seen the video " The Best Things" by Filter, then you wouod see me and all my buddies cars in the vid. My friend's 66 Olds 442 ( black car with red crow on the hood ) was used for the vid, and because the set director like the look of all of our cars ( he is the dad of another of my buddies ) we were asked to have all our cars in the vid  - a few of my friends got pissed because the set director didnt want any mustangs, he wanted true muscle cars - that made us feel great =-)<P> So while on the set we met all the band members, me and Richy Patric ( lead singer ) got drunk off our asses and started doing burnouts in the middle of the desert, unfortunately they werent filming that part - as folks would have seen him roll over the go-for truck =-)<P><BR>Once also met Rob Zombie - damn cool guy, completely different from what I expected him to be. <P>Met Pauly Shore when he was filming Bio-dome up at my old high school ( Valencia ), wanted to just punch him in the face, annoying as hell<P><BR>Met a few stars, but cannot recall them all<BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000059||Pontiaddict||08-30-2001||12:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>If any of you guys have seen the video " The Best Things" by Filter, then you wouod see me and all my buddies cars in the vid. My friend's 66 Olds 442 ( black car with red crow on the hood ) was used for the vid, and because the set director like the look of all of our cars ( he is the dad of another of my buddies ) we were asked to have all our cars in the vid  - a few of my friends got pissed because the set director didnt want any mustangs, he wanted true muscle cars - that made us feel great =-)<P> So while on the set we met all the band members, me and Richy Patric ( lead singer ) got drunk off our asses and started doing burnouts in the middle of the desert, unfortunately they werent filming that part - as folks would have seen him roll over the go-for truck =-)<P><BR>Once also met Rob Zombie - damn cool guy, completely different from what I expected him to be. <P>Met Pauly Shore when he was filming Bio-dome up at my old high school ( Valencia ), wanted to just punch him in the face, annoying as hell<P><BR>Met a few stars, but cannot recall them all<BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cool||||reg||1
Z||000060||fierohoho||08-30-2001||11:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake_Dragon:<BR><B>Any one remember   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://4.43.132.133/cf/dpb/dpb04b.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sooooooooooo Jake, I'm loosing sleep.<BR>Who is this and why does he exist?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000061||Formula88||08-30-2001||12:01 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>[whisper]he's got 2 roles... he's a man in black and another *secret* role[/whisper]    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nuts!  That is SOO cool!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  We should get a group together to catch the opening of the movie!<P>My brush with fame?  Well, if Astronauts count, I used to work for NASA and met a bunch.  Almost got a ride in a T-38 with one, but he decided not to risk it.  He'd had his Astronaut wings revoked for 6 months for breaking the sound barrier too close to populated areas.  That bumped him from a space flight.  This was his first flight after having been re-instated, so he wasn't about to screw it up!  It's real easy to tell which Astronauts are scientists and which are military.  Especially the Naval Aviators.  Those dudes are CRAZY!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Love partying with them!<P>As for regular celebs, I met David Lee Roth backstage after a Van Halen concert once (I was interviewing him for my school newspaper).  He was an A$$!  <P>I've met a bunch of celebs/actors at Sci-Fi Conventions, but that's different.  At one convention, we had Kane Hodder, Gunner Hanson, and Doug Bradley.  They were partying and drinking together one night - the Unholy Trinity of Horror: Jason, Leatherface, and Pinhead, all in the same room!  That was cool.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000062||Raydar||08-30-2001||12:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>  ...As for regular celebs, I met David Lee Roth...  He was an A$$!  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gee. What a surprise.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000063||sqoach||08-30-2001||01:08 PM||||Well, with my trip to California, I got to see a few famous people. Went to the Tonight Show. Was sitting really close to Kevin Eubanks. Jesse Ventura was a guest on the show that day.<P>Hey, have any of you been watching the Dallas Cowboys? Look for a rookie named Lynn Scott. I'm pretty sure he starts, or at least plays. He use to go to college here in Alva, and was an All-American. I met him a few times. He's a nice guy. I shoulda got his autograph  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
