Z||000070||Cheever3000||09-01-2001||10:22 PM||||You know the chubby security guard in Ernest Goes to Jail?  Of course you don't.  He was the cook in Ernest Goes to Camp.  No?  Okay, he was the Big Bopper in The Buddy Holly Story with Gary Busey.  Well he lived next door to me when I was a baby.  He & my big brother played together.  His dad was a firefighter, same as mine.  Maybe that one doesn't knock your socks off, but it means something to me.<P>His name is Gaylord Sartain.  He & Busey did a late-night live weekly local TV show in Tulsa soon after high school, and it was hysterical.  Later, Gaylord was on the Hee Haw show (Sound familiar, Songman?).  Funny guy.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000071||GodSend||09-02-2001||12:12 AM||||A couple of years ago I got to make breakfest for a few ex nhlers at my old chef job.  I made a 3 egg omlette with Ham, Onion, and Green peppers for Bobby Hull (Johnny Bower was there too).<P>  Best this is a got to go out and talk to them.  I sat down with Bobby for a few minutes.  I asked him if I had seen the leafs game last night(playoffs 2 years ago)... he laughed and said - No way, my son was playing... then he turned to the sports section where the title said BRETT HULL IS ONE MAN WRECKING CREW .. I replied...-Hrmm.. never heard of him!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000072||FieroKyle||09-02-2001||01:14 AM||||I saw Dale Earnhardt from a distance at Michigan Speedway a couple years back. It was in the Garage area.||||reg||1
Z||000073||frontal lobe||09-02-2001||10:59 PM||||Met Reggie Roby at U. of Iowa-he later punted for the Dolphins.<P>Walked right by Magic Johnson on the basketball court at U. of Iowa when he was at Michigan State.<P>Stood right next to Ralph Sampson at the Final Four 1981.  TALL and SKINNY.<P>Shook hands with UNC legend Dean Smith after a Marquette game due to going to medical school with Joe Wolf's sister.  Very cordial man even though he must have met a bazillion people in his life.<P>Marquette legend Al Maguire and Wis. state senator Herb Kohl rubbed by baby daughter's head in a Denny's.  Both very nice.  Part of the job for a politician, I guess.<P>Had this scintillating conversation with Nolan Ryan when I was about 13-over the outfield wall:  "Hey Nolan, when are you pitching again?"  Nolan:  "Not for 2 more days."  He was nice about it.<P>Stood at a crosswalk right next to the U.S. capitol building waiting for the light to change, right next to Senator Ted Kennedy for about 30+ seconds.  I refused to acknowledge him for fear I would heckle him, and am proud to say I stood there silently and did not bring up Chappaquidick (spelling?), alcoholism, or the exquisite irony of him being on the ethics committee||||reg||1
Z||000074||Jimmy||09-03-2001||03:17 AM||||Met Destinys Child (Kelly Rowland) at the Voodoo Lounge in Vegas this past week. My college buds and I met the DJ from Bloodhound Gang, he invited us to go to a couple of tour dates with them on their bus, we did.  And I know a couple of old MN Twins players. <P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000075||Cheever3000||09-03-2001||11:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>scintillating conversation with Nolan Ryan</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>He passed me on State Highway 6 just outside of his Alvin Texas hometown.  It was him alright.  I was in my minivan, he was driving a new black Grand Prix.<P>||||reg||6
